{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider bears the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has discharged it on an unimpaired trace: the deviation derived from EV-GPS-09111 reports status 'established', an excess of 4.2 km against an optimal route of 12.0 km (35.00%), which passes both POL-RD-01 gates (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km). The driver's own case therefore cannot be that nothing happened: the deviation is measured, and the rider's entitlement is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic and nothing beyond it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09111", "EV-TRIP-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The materiality gates in POL-RD-01 are that an excess is 'additionally MATERIAL' only where it exceeds 50% of the optimal distance or 8.0 km absolute. Here the derived excess is 35.00% and 4.2 km, so neither gate is met: the deviation is established but NOT material. The consequence is that the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is never triggered, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and the driver's monetary exposure is capped at the ordinary POL-RD-02 recomputation. The policy uses the word 'material' as a defined threshold, not as a description of how the rider felt about the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09111", "EV-TRIP-09111", "EV-FARE-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if materiality were reached, POL-RD-06 requires a repeat pattern measured exclusively on driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d. On this record deviation_flags_90d is 0 and completed_trips_90d is 610, so the clause's own two gates (3 or more flags, or a ratio of 0.05 or more) fail: 0 divided by 610 is 0. There is no pattern on this record, and the two effects of POL-RD-06 that would hurt the driver - the FULL_REFUND uplift and the driver-conduct referral - are both unavailable. The driver's lifetime counter and his 90-day flag count agree at zero.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No exculpatory clause rescues the excess, and the driver does not pretend otherwise. The rider's only chat message asks for a return to the booked route - 'The navigation route was left after Pioneer Road. Please return to the booked route.' That is the opposite of a rider-requested detour, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable, and its corroboration test cannot even be run because waypoint_hint is null and no road is named in the rider's message. There is no amendment of either endpoint and neither amended_optimal_distance_km nor amended_optimal_duration_min is populated, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09111", "EV-TRIP-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": null,
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's statement that he 'followed the road available to me' asserts an external traffic cause but names no advisory. The bundle's only traffic artifact, EV-ADVIS-09111-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and a BLOCKING MISSING_ARTIFACT issue, so no advisory covers this trip window and POL-RD-03 is unavailable on the record. Under POL-RD-13(2) the assertion is accordingly discarded and carries no weight under POL-RD-08; and because the driver cites no evidence ID for an advisory - there is none to cite - the absence is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger. The case is therefore ruled, not escalated: the excess stands at the measured 4.2 km against the booked optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09111-01", "EV-GPS-09111", "EV-TRIP-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": null,
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only affirmative monetary claim fails on the record and I concede it: POL-RD-04 permits DRIVER_COMPENSATION at SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre only where the fare_breakdown bills the rider for less distance than the gps_trace records and the shortfall exceeds 1.0 km. Here the billed distance is 16.2 km and the trace distance is 16.2 km - a shortfall of zero - so no compensation is available. The 1.00 SGD ERP line for the Pioneer Road inbound gantry is on the optimal route and properly chargeable under POL-RD-09, and the 2.00 SGD Tuas South Avenue 8 loop line is carried here for completeness only, as a pass-through line already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund and not some further sum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09111", "EV-TRIP-09111", "EV-GPS-09111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 9.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this dispute is decided on the trip's own GPS trace and the fare arithmetic, and it produces a partial refund of SGD 9.15 to the rider. Deviation. The GPS trace EV-GPS-09111 (weight 1.0; 205 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps) measures 16.2 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff; the booked optimal route on EV-TRIP-09111 is 12.0 km. The excess is 4.2 km, or 35.0% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates pass (above 20% and above 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not reach the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gates, so it is not MATERIAL: no POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is required, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and no driver-conduct referral arises. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), so the deviation stands on the trace alone and no corroboration is needed. The driver's answer. The statement that he 'followed the road available to me' is an external-cause assertion with no advisory behind it. The only traffic artifact, EV-ADVIS-09111-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and covers nothing, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-13, the assertion carries no weight. Because no advisory evidence ID was cited, this is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. No rider-requested detour was made: the rider's only message asks the driver to return to the booked route, and no endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 do not apply. The refund. The fare model is METERED and there is no quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 does not apply and POL-RD-02 governs. Recomputed fare on the booked optimal = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 12.0 km + 0.28 x 24.0 min) x 1.2 surge (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) = 23.424, + 0.80 platform fee + 1.00 ERP for the on-optimal Pioneer Road inbound gantry - 1.00 promo discount = 24.224. Charged total = 33.36. Refund = 33.36 - 24.224 = 9.136, rounded up to SGD 9.15. ERP. The Tuas South Avenue 8 loop line (2.00) is off-route pass-through; it is itemised here for transparency but is already comprehended in the recomputed fare, which includes only on-route gantries, so it is NOT added on top of the 9.15 (POL-RD-09(1)). The Pioneer Road inbound line (1.00) is properly chargeable and sits inside the recomputed fare. Outcome. The refund is above the 0.50 de minimis and is 27.4% of the charged total, below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND. It happens to equal the whole contested amount, but POL-RD-02's test for a full refund is the share of the charged total, which is not met. No driver compensation is due: the distance billed (16.2 km) equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04. No profile field other than deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d is used as a ground of decision; the remaining profile data is context only."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

